175
00:09:38,439 --> 00:09:39,640
What's a vigilante?

176
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,360
What does that mean?

177
00:09:41,719 --> 00:09:45,719
Well, there's sort of three kinds of membership in order of the arrow.

178
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,439
You can be an ordeal member,

179
00:09:48,439 --> 00:09:51,400
which is basically anyone who's in the organization.

180
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,719
There's no really special privileges.

181
00:09:53,719 --> 00:09:55,480
but if you're serious about it

182
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,000
and want to continue to be involved

183
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,400
after you've been in for a year,

184
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,320
you can go on to become a brotherhood member,

185
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:05,000
which is open to anyone that is in the order of the arrow

186
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,960
that chooses to be.

187
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:11,720
Beyond that, a lodge can select a small number of people each year

188
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,480
to become vigilante members.

189
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:17,560
It's just a recognition really, for service,

190
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:20,120
not necessarily in the lodge, but in scouts.

191
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:24,680
The rules are that you have to select

192
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,960
at least as many youth as you do adults,

193
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,640
so you can't just pack it with adults.

194
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:34,760
And the actual selection of who gets honored is the voting is

195
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,800
youth members only.

196
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:39,320
So the adults that get in are the ones that are

197
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,720
recognized by the youth in their lodge

198
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,560
as being useful in some way.

199
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:50,840
Now, how does a scout become a member of the order of the arrow?

200
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,760
Well, they get elected by the members of their troop.

201
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:57,000
There's some basic eligibility criteria:

202
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,920
You have to have a certain number of days of camping.

203
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:00,920
You have to be a first class scout.

204
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,680
You have to have attended a long-term camp

205
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:03,560
like a summer camp.

206
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,280
Once you become eligible,

207
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:10,200
each troop can have an election once each year.

208
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,560
It's a little unique in that the whole troop gets to vote,

209
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,840
not just OA members.

210
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,520
So membership is not determined by the membership

211
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:21,720
but instead by the broader body of scouting

212
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:26,840
And the idea is that it's supposed to be an honor camper

213
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:30,840
kind of a thing where they're supposed to vote for those

214
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:35,400
who they believe are good scouts and deserving of it

215
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,600
And if they're elected then they have

216
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,880
a year to complete the ordeal,

217
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:45,160
which is basically a kind of a weekend induction.

218
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,880
After that they're actually members.

219
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:49,160
Until then they're just candidates

220
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:53,880
And that's the induction weekend.

221
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,480
That's an ordeal weekend.

222
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,480
I hear that term used a lot,

223
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,840
Correct.

224
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,960
Well, different lodges call it different things,

225
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,560
but that's sort of the generic term.

226
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:06,600
So ours we call it the spring or the fall assembly.

227
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,760
It's the official name of the event,

228
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,520
But what it is is the ordeal weekend

229
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:13,240
or the weekend at which they complete the ordeal.

230
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:18,600
And Larry, you were made a lodge member

231
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,920
as a youth in scouting.

232
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:27,000
Yes, I was elected at about 15 or 16,

233
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:32,920
but I wasn't a brotherhood member until an adult.

234
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,640
And what about you, Tom?

235
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,319
Same thing.

236
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,280
I was elected as a youth

237
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:44,760
And when my sons got involved in scouting

238
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,200
I learned more.

239
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,840
I got re-involved with everything

240
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:52,200
and did the brotherhood ceremony.

241
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:57,640
My boys got involved with the ceremonies team.

242
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,880
I was helping them with the ceremonies teams

243
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:05,560
And in that process they elected me

244
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:09,240
into the vigilante through the lodge.

245
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,720
So ceremonies have a big.

246
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:15,800
they're a big part of the order there, aren't they?

247
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,120
Yes,

248
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,560
And very much so.

249
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,360
What function do they have?

250
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,760
They tell the story of the OA.

251
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,000
They tell the story of the Delaware Indians.

252
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:33,160
They have all the symbolisms that the OA represents

253
00:13:33,719 --> 00:13:37,959
And they're pretty cool to watch

254
00:13:37,959 --> 00:13:40,520
when you can stand back and watch them

255
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,719
and know what's going on.

256
00:13:41,719 --> 00:13:46,120
They're sort of a very unique aspect of Boy Scouts.

257
00:13:46,839 --> 00:13:52,040
I was inducted into the order as an adult, like you, TW,

258
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,160
And I was a scoutmaster at the time

259
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,319
And so we have a little bit of a different story

260
00:13:57,319 --> 00:13:58,520
than Tom and Larry do.

261
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:03,240
But what I often hear is some scoutmasters

262
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,280
and scout leaders are a little concerned

263
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,720
about the order of the arrow,

264
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,720
kind of sapping the attention of their older scouts

265
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,680
away from working with the troop and things like that.

266
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,960
Has that been your experience?

267
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,480
No, it really hasn't.

268
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,120
In fact it's, if anything, gone the other way.

269
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:22,680
But that really depends on the attitude

270
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,040
of the scoutmaster and the troop.

271
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:28,199
We chose in our troop to embrace the OA

272
00:14:28,199 --> 00:14:33,319
as another set of activities for interested scouts.

273
00:14:33,319 --> 00:14:35,160
We tried to support OA,

274
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:38,040
make sure that we didn't schedule troop campouts

275
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,560
in conflict with OA events.

276
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:44,040
We provided transportation to OA assemblies,

277
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,959
just like we did to troop campouts and stuff,

278
00:14:45,959 --> 00:14:49,160
And as a result, really I think it strengthened us

279
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:52,439
and kept some of our older boys engaged.

280
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:55,000
Certainly some of them decided it was cool

281
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,160
to go out and assist with assemblies

282
00:14:57,160 --> 00:15:01,480
and spend a few extra nights camping as a result.

283
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:04,360
So the other thing that I think is overlooked a lot

284
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:07,400
is boys are youths in the OA until they turn 21..

285
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,560
One of the things that makes Boy Scouting work

286
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,160
is the older scout role model-

287
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:14,280
a younger scout being able to look up to an older scout

288
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:16,920
that he wants to be like.

289
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,680
And you reach a point where you run out of that

290
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:21,080
in the troop because the older boys

291
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,400
are the older boys.

292
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,320
They don't have anyone to look up to

293
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,800
And yet sometimes they can find that in the OA.

294
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,200
Certainly that was the case, for both of my sons

295
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,600
Ended up really adopting role models

296
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,760
that were guys that they knew in the lodge

297
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,240
that were competent older scouts

298
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,760
that were a couple of years older than them

299
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:42,920
when they were the older boys in the troop,

300
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:44,680
And I think that's a strength that troops

301
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,240
can get from it. that is often overlooked.

302
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:49,080
Tom and Larry- kind of the same question

303
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:55,080
As scout masters, were you concerned about that type of thing

304
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,000
And what was the ultimate result

305
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,120
of watching your boys get involved with the OA?

306
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:05,000
As scout master I did very much like TW does.

307
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:08,040
I put on the calendar when the OA events are,

308
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:10,040
so we don't. when they do their planning

309
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:15,640
they don't overwrite something that is an OA weekend

310
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:21,319
And I use the OA in the troop as the service arm

311
00:16:21,319 --> 00:16:23,800
of the troop or for the district. sometimes

312
00:16:24,439 --> 00:16:26,360
We may be called upon to do something.

313
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,240
I get to let the OA rep know

314
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:32,199
and he gets his guys together and off they go.

315
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,120
So it's a. it functions pretty well.

316
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:39,160
I've never- I've always- supported the ordeal,

317
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:42,600
but I haven't really supported the other activities

318
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,960
as much as a scout master.

319
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:46,600
I've kind of left that to the guys in the troop to decide

320
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:48,920
what they want to do.

321
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:53,160
My experience has been sometimes that the OA

322
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:57,960
and the district have a tendency to pull adults out,

323
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,680
and not regularly or often, but occasionally,

324
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:06,440
And I don't know that that's always bad.

325
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:09,720
Our troop, the guys, are always free to go

326
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,839
to the local log chapter meetings,

327
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,600
you know, go to lodge events,

328
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:18,280
but I haven't had a lot of guys for whatever reason

329
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,960
I guess, just haven't done that.

330
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:23,400
Well, one of the interesting things about a scout

331
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,079
that gets involved in the order of the arrow,

332
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:27,000
he pretty much does it on his terms.

333
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:32,200
He doesn't have to go as part of a troop or patrol

334
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,080
to participate.

335
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:36,280
He's basically he's doing this pretty much individually,

336
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:36,840
wouldn't you say-

337
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,000
In my case, yes,

338
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,720
Yeah, ours too pretty much.

339
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,480
Has that been your experience, TW,

340
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:47,320
that the boys are more or less doing this on their own terms?

341
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:47,960
Yeah, absolutely,

342
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:48,760
It's optional,

343
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:51,640
It's something that they can do to the extent they want.

344
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:53,240
Some of them will go through their ordeal

345
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,720
and never go back because it didn't click.

346
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:59,560
Some of them will decide it's the greatest thing ever

347
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:00,840
and they'll want to do everything

348
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,000
and you know, must them or somewhere in between.

349
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,960
One of the other things: I think that really works.

350
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:08,360
we talked a minute ago about ceremonies.

351
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,840
ceremonies in OA really try to restate the values

352
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,840
that we have in scouting around- leadership

353
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,680
and self-reliance and stuff.

354
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:19,640
And I've seen a few cases where there was a boy

355
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:22,360
that kind of wasn't getting it in the troop context

356
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:24,680
and somehow hearing it from a different direction

357
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:27,560
kind of worked for him and engaged him.

358
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:30,600
So the other thing I liked about it as a scout master:

359
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,880
it was a way of kind of restating the stuff

360
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:36,040
that we've been trying to get through to them

361
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,400
from a different perspective

362
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,720
And sometimes when you hear it from a different direction

363
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,040
it kind of sinks in better.

364
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,280
Yeah, I've always seen it as a very positive thing

365
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:45,320
for our scouts.

366
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:46,120
They get involved.

367
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:48,440
They get involved at the level that they want to.

368
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:53,160
I've had scouts involved on the OA Executive Committee

369
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:57,080
and who have been officers in the lodge

370
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:59,320
And I guess some of this

371
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,160
we're kind of running over some of these terms.

372
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:04,120
but how has a lodge constituted? TW,

373
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,000
How does that work?

374
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:08,440
Talk to me about officers and things like that for a moment.

375
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:13,240
Well, the lodge is basically the council level unit of the OA.

376
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:15,960
if you will just like in a troop,

377
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:17,880
There's a youth and an adult staff.

378
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:20,440
You have a lodge advisor, who's the adult leader,

379
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,320
that's kind of responsible for keeping them out of trouble

380
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:23,720
and stuff,

381
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,360
And then you have an elected lodge chief,

382
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,880
who's the senior youth leader,

383
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,440
who then has a set of vice chiefs

384
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:32,120
for various functions like service.

385
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:35,400
In our lodge at least, those are annually

386
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,320
elected, annually at the spring assembly

387
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,560
And I think that's pretty typical.

388
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:45,960
And then they run a- we call it a lodge executive committee.

389
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:49,320
Those youth officers run monthly meetings or so

390
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:51,640
to try to keep things going

391
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:54,440
And, like in any other scouting thing,

392
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,360
they're the ones that are supposed to be running the lodge

393
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:57,720
and running the events.

394
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:00,600
The adults provide some continuity and some reminders

395
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,760
about the stuff they need to get done.

396
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,360
But generally it works pretty well

397
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:06,280
And one of the advantages the OA has

398
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:09,640
is that the youth can still be youth until they turn 21..

399
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:11,720
So some of the boys that have aged out of their troop

400
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,160
but still want to have a leadership role

401
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,440
can find something to do there

402
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,080
And they're old enough to actually be pretty good at it.

403
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,160
So a lot of times that works pretty well.

404
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:21,000
I agree with TW:

405
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:26,440
The older scouts: once they turn 18 and continue on,

406
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,600
they do excel.

407
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:33,640
They understand what's supposed to be happening

408
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,560
and they make it happen pretty much.

409
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:37,640
It's pretty amazing to watch.

410
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:41,480
Years and years ago everything about the ceremonies

411
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,640
and the different things about the lodge

412
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,120
were kind of considered to be a secret.

413
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:49,560
just in the way of openness and youth protection.

414
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:51,960
Those things were no longer considered

415
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,880
to be closely guarded secrets.

416
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:57,880
If a parent or a leader or somebody is concerned

417
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:00,680
about what's going on at an OA weekend,

418
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:03,720
I mean we do call it in some places an ordeal weekend

419
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,160
and that's kind of caught the attention

420
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:08,520
of a couple of parents over the years with my troop

421
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,920
and they've wondered what exactly that means

422
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:13,960
Or if they're interested in what the content

423
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,120
of the ceremonies or something like that is.

424
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:20,360
the proceedings of the order they are

425
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:22,040
are no longer secret, are they,

426
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:25,480
I think, for adults? as far as I'm concerned,

427
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,240
if you want to see what's going on,

428
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:29,080
I think that's the scouting way now.

429
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:32,520
Now for scouts, there aren't any secrets,

430
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:34,120
There's only surprises.

431
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:36,760
We asked the scouts that are ordeal members

432
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:39,879
not to just blab around.

433
00:21:39,879 --> 00:21:41,399
It's not a secret exactly,

434
00:21:41,399 --> 00:21:44,200
but we don't lay it out for them

435
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,760
like we lay out some other campouts or things.

436
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:47,480
We just kind of keep it.

437
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,120
It's guarded,

438
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:49,399
Yeah,

439
00:21:49,399 --> 00:21:51,320
It's just a guarded knowledge.

440
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:53,800
We tend to have a couple of different reactions.

441
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,320
if a parent wants to go look,

442
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:58,680
First of all we try to explain to them what's going on

443
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,720
and make, help them understand

444
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,040
that their kid's not going to be in trouble or anything.

445
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:06,120
But if it's an adult that is involved as a leader

446
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:08,360
and that might someday themselves go through it,

447
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,080
we try to encourage them not to do it and save it-

448
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:16,680
Surprise was the word used- and let it unfold

449
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,680
when they get to go through it.

450
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,440
If it's really a parent that's not very involved,

451
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,080
probably not ever going to be into NOA,

452
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:25,160
and they really want to go watch, that's okay.

453
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:31,480
But at the same time this is kind of a getting older scout thing

454
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:33,800
And it's one of those things that really

455
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:35,160
he doesn't need mom's help for

456
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:41,080
And mom certainly has the right to go and watch mom or dad

457
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:42,200
if they want.

458
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:45,240
But at the same time the boy really deserves the chance

459
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,240
to do this on his own if that's what he wants,

460
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,280
And I usually- I've been through a couple of times

461
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:53,000
when I kind of tried to interpret that for a parent.

462
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:57,080
I would never prevent a parent that wanted to go and you can't.

463
00:22:57,080 --> 00:23:00,520
BSA has no secret organizations and Youth Protection says

464
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,520
the parent has the right to be there.

465
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:04,360
But I would try to explain to them why

466
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:05,720
maybe they don't want to be there

467
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:08,440
and maybe it's not for the best if they're there

468
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,240
And if at the end of that they feel like they got to go, that's fine.

469
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:21,240
I've had parents question what's in the ceremony and what kind of wording

470
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:21,960
and stuff like that.

471
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:28,280
I just show them the ceremony book and let them read the parts

472
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:29,560
and see what's in it.

473
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,360
Yeah, if you look at the ordeal ceremony,

474
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:34,680
it's really surprising to some people

475
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:37,240
how much it's based on the scout oath and the scout law,

476
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:38,120
if you pay attention.

477
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:38,760
Right,

478
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,280
Very much so,

479
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:44,360
And I think that's a good strategy for a parent

480
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:46,360
that wants to understand what they're being told

481
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,640
and what's involved.

482
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:53,000
I've also had- we had a troop in town that the church

483
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,200
they were chartered to had concerns about it being

484
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,040
some kind of weird Indian religious thing

485
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:01,320
And helping them. first of all,

486
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:04,280
all the major churches have signed off on this

487
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:05,240
so years ago.

488
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:08,280
But second of all, having them read the ceremony

489
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,040
and look at what they actually say

490
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:13,560
And they find it's very consistent with scouting values

491
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:17,000
And it kind of defused that whole thing.

492
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:19,000
That's cool.

493
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:19,640
Yeah,

494
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:22,760
I've never had anything like that from up above.

495
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:23,720
That's pretty cool.

496
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:26,360
Sometimes a new scout leader or a new scout master

497
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:28,040
will be faced with somebody saying:

498
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:30,360
you know it's time for you to have your OA election.

499
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:33,160
TW, have you been a part of running those elections

500
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:33,720
in the past?

501
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:37,400
You certainly have had them conducted for you

502
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:38,440
at a scout meeting.

503
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:39,880
Sure,

504
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:42,840
I've actually helped from the chapter side

505
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:45,160
run elections and other troops as well.

506
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:49,320
What's my role as a scout master in an OA election.

507
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:51,640
Beyond basic eligibility, the scout master

508
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:54,680
is supposed to give sort of a scout spirit: sign off

509
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:58,520
So you could, if you chose, eliminate.

510
00:24:58,520 --> 00:25:00,440
if you had a kid with a really bad attitude

511
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:04,040
or some issue, you could keep them off the ballot.

512
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:06,040
My experience is that's probably a bad idea

513
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,040
because the kids that are going to vote

514
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:10,040
understand just fine what they need to do

515
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,880
and that that's not the right person to elect.

516
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:14,920
So I have never done that myself.

517
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:17,640
What about you, Tom or Larry?

518
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:19,400
Has that ever been an issue for you?

519
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:22,200
Generally, the scout master should look at the guys

520
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:25,400
that are eligible by number of days, camping

521
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:28,760
and first class and whatnot, and just sign them off.

522
00:25:28,840 --> 00:25:31,160
But other than that, leave it to the boys.

523
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:34,520
I do specifically ask the candidates

524
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:35,800
that are going to be elected:

525
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:39,640
Do they want to go into the to be elected?

526
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:41,800
That's a good point.

527
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:45,480
If they don't have any want to do that,

528
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,720
there's no need in having them on the ballot anyway.

529
00:25:47,720 --> 00:25:50,760
So I just make sure that they understand

530
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:54,040
that they are getting ready to go through the election process.

531
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,040
That's a good point.

532
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:59,399
They certainly don't have to be on the ballot

533
00:25:59,399 --> 00:26:00,200
if they don't want to.

534
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:03,399
I've had a couple that not many,

535
00:26:03,399 --> 00:26:05,080
but a couple through the years that didn't want to.

536
00:26:05,639 --> 00:26:07,560
The other thing I discovered about elections

537
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:09,879
is that in any kind of a large troop,

538
00:26:09,879 --> 00:26:11,960
as in a troop with two or more patrols,

539
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:13,560
the boys have no idea what the names

540
00:26:13,560 --> 00:26:15,000
of half the people in the troop are.

541
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:19,320
One of the things that we started doing years ago now-

542
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:23,240
based on, I think I got the idea from Calvin Gray-

543
00:26:23,240 --> 00:26:25,880
is having a photo ballot.

544
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:27,720
They know the other boys,

545
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,480
they have an impression of their behavior

546
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:32,200
and what good scouts they are,

547
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:33,800
but they don't know the names of the kids

548
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,800
that are not in their patrol necessarily,

549
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:40,520
And we've started having much better election results

550
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:41,960
when they could actually look at the picture

551
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,160
of who they're voting for,

552
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:46,520
rather than trying to remember some kid's name- who

553
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:48,680
out of 30 or 40 kids.

554
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:52,120
they can't keep the names all straight.

555
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:54,280
So I think that's really helped the quality

556
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,320
of our OA elections.

557
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:59,720
We've gone and had the candidates

558
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:03,160
sit across the front of the gym.

559
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:04,840
These are the ones,

560
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:06,680
these are who you're going to be voting on,

561
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,320
But we don't. you know,

562
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:10,760
that's as far as we go on that.

563
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:12,520
That's a pretty good idea, though

564
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:13,560
We used to do the same thing.

565
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:14,600
We'd have them line up there.

566
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,600
we'd have their names written on the board

567
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:19,080
and still it's just hard for them to keep them straight

568
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:24,280
And this way they can associate their vote directly

569
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:27,000
with you know, knowing exactly who they're voting

570
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:27,879
or not voting for.

571
00:27:28,760 --> 00:27:29,800
Ever since we've done that,

572
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:31,639
I've the kids that get elected

573
00:27:31,639 --> 00:27:33,000
are the ones that are.

574
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,320
we get a pretty decent number of kids elected,

575
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:36,840
but they're the right kids.

576
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:39,480
TW, thank you so much for spending the time with us.

577
00:27:39,480 --> 00:27:41,000
We really do appreciate it.

578
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,439
It's been a pleasure. I've enjoyed it.

579
00:27:42,439 --> 00:27:44,600
Yeah, And we'll look forward maybe

580
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:45,800
to having you back someday

581
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:47,720
when Walter is on vacation again.

582
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:48,840
Aloha, Walter,

583
00:27:49,159 --> 00:27:50,439
If you're listening in,

584
00:27:50,439 --> 00:27:52,600
But thanks again, TW.

585
00:27:52,600 --> 00:27:53,800
All right, catch you later.

586
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:54,919
Good night, TW,

587
00:27:54,919 --> 00:27:55,720
See you.

588
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,919
See you later.

589
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:16,919
So we're going to welcome Blaise, Vitale

590
00:28:16,919 --> 00:28:18,520
and Blaise, where are you from?

591
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,800
Currently from Grantsford, Wisconsin,

592
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:23,080
Grantsford, Wisconsin,

593
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:24,360
And you're a scout master.

594
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:25,560
Yes,

595
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:27,159
And what's your troop number there?

596
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,399
560..

597
00:28:29,399 --> 00:28:33,399
560 is a brand new troop of guys

598
00:28:33,399 --> 00:28:35,000
who were Weebelos a year or so ago.

599
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:35,560
Is that right?

600
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:38,360
Half of the troop was Weebelos

601
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:41,240
and half of the troop was not scouts.

602
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:42,199
Oh, okay.

603
00:28:42,199 --> 00:28:43,000
Okay,

604
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,679
I've got a first year troop

605
00:28:44,679 --> 00:28:46,600
and I've been trying to teach them lashings.

606
00:28:47,320 --> 00:28:49,400
We were supposed to make a sled

607
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,320
for our district's contact derby,

608
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,920
and I figured that was a perfect opportunity

609
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:53,960
to do this.

610
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:55,240
The scouts made a few attempts

611
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:56,920
and then gradually all abandoned the sled

612
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,680
to go back, go play a game,

613
00:28:58,680 --> 00:29:00,840
and then the sled was left unfinished.

614
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:02,920
I was torn at that point

615
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,440
between just letting the scouts fail

616
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,960
and possibly canceling the derby.

617
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:07,720
But with a young troop,

618
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:09,480
I really tried to give them the opportunities

619
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:12,440
to succeed because, in fairness,

620
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:13,960
the leaders weren't really prepared.

621
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,640
I called another meeting,

622
00:29:16,120 --> 00:29:18,360
essentially bribed my scouts with pizza

623
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:19,720
if they came and worked on the sled,

624
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:22,600
But I don't know,

625
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:26,120
did I overstep letting the boys run the show?

626
00:29:26,120 --> 00:29:28,280
I'm trying to develop this boy-led troop,

627
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:31,400
but I often feel like I'm running the whole show

628
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:33,000
and my boys aren't really stepping up.

629
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:35,960
Well, how many boys all together Blaze?

630
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:39,800
At that point I only had eight scouts

631
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:41,640
and six of them were there that night

632
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:45,560
And most of them are 11 or 12 years old.

633
00:29:46,760 --> 00:29:47,320
Yes,

634
00:29:47,320 --> 00:29:48,680
And it's a brand new troop.

635
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,840
Well, we're almost a year old,

636
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:53,560
Almost a year old, but still kind of brand new.

637
00:29:53,560 --> 00:29:55,320
Okay, so that gives us a little background

638
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:56,360
to deal with the question.

639
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,720
And is this your first experience

640
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:00,840
as a leader in scouting?

641
00:30:02,280 --> 00:30:04,840
Well, I was a Weeblow leader, but yes,

642
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:07,160
and I was not a scout myself,

643
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:09,960
so the lashings were alien to me.

644
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:16,120
So I think my guess is that the three of us

645
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:17,080
have been there before

646
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:18,840
and we're going to do our best to get you

647
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,600
through the situation here a little bit.

648
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,680
Who'd like to start?

649
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:26,760
Well, Blaze, did you have an annual planning conference?

650
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:30,200
Not for this past year,

651
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:32,360
We're going to be having one very soon.

652
00:30:32,360 --> 00:30:34,440
I can't get that. my boys are very excited

653
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:35,880
about doing that kind of stuff.

654
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:38,520
If they make the annual plan

655
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:41,160
and they put the Klondike Derby in there,

656
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,920
that starts the process of it being theirs.

657
00:30:45,879 --> 00:30:47,879
If you made this plan and said,

658
00:30:47,879 --> 00:30:49,560
well, the district's having this

659
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:50,760
and our troops going to go,

660
00:30:51,879 --> 00:30:53,240
then it's not theirs

661
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:57,800
And for whatever reason,

662
00:30:57,800 --> 00:31:00,440
they decided not to get behind that

663
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,440
without you pushing them,

664
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:04,440
Although at the same point,

665
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:07,960
I've also heard that we're supposed to be looking

666
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:10,360
for whatever initiative they're showing.

667
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,960
Last year we went as weeblos to this same event

668
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:15,720
and they definitely said they wanted to go again.

669
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:17,880
So I'm using whatever spark of initiative

670
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:19,320
they wanted to go to this

671
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,480
And to do that. this instead of borrowing,

672
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:23,080
is that we had to make one

673
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:24,600
Right? Well, that's fine,

674
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,840
I mean, but somewhere along the way

675
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:30,520
they start deciding what they want to do

676
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:35,160
and they start getting excited about their program.

677
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,880
Where you want to be is where they are saying,

678
00:31:37,880 --> 00:31:39,640
hey, that's where we want to go,

679
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:40,600
That's what we want to do.

680
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:43,640
But it's not just your troop.

681
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,800
We've been a stout master for 18 years.

682
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:47,640
The troop is 18 years old

683
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,880
Right now. we've got 32 boys.

684
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:52,760
In December, there was a planning conference

685
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:55,880
and they were going to go skiing this weekend,

686
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,880
but there's no snow around here this year,

687
00:31:57,880 --> 00:32:01,160
So they decided to go to the winter campery,

688
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:02,280
the district campery,

689
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:04,680
which was also scheduled for this weekend.

690
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:09,560
Two weeks ago. they had not even talked about it.

691
00:32:09,560 --> 00:32:13,000
It was still. they had the, they had the fliers,

692
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,080
but they had not even talked about it,

693
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:16,440
And it was driving me crazy.

694
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:19,800
They did start talking about it this past Monday.

695
00:32:20,520 --> 00:32:23,720
There was more planning, permission slips were taken up

696
00:32:23,720 --> 00:32:29,000
And and we were taken 15,

697
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:32,040
15 scouts to the campery this weekend.

698
00:32:32,040 --> 00:32:34,040
So they did it.

699
00:32:34,520 --> 00:32:37,320
We don't know what's. I don't know what's going to happen once, for there.

700
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:41,320
There may be a four hour breakfast, but we are going.

701
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:48,200
So it they. I was sitting back and the other adults were sitting back

702
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:51,480
waiting for them to do something about it,

703
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,600
And they finally did.

704
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:56,520
How much did it take to keep you in your seat on that?

705
00:32:57,720 --> 00:32:58,520
Quite a bit of rope,

706
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,440
Quite a bit of duct tape.

707
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:04,920
And listen to Mr Geiger and Mr Green.

708
00:33:05,640 --> 00:33:09,800
What you're talking about, Blaze, is, is a familiar story.

709
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:11,000
It's very familiar.

710
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:15,160
Let me ask you, Tom and Larry- these guys are 11 or 12 years old-

711
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,520
What's the factor there?

712
00:33:16,520 --> 00:33:18,920
Well, they're not as interested in planning

713
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:21,560
And you're going to, and you're going to be frustrated by that,

714
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:23,080
And that's OK.

715
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:28,600
You can make suggestions about some places to go and some things to do,

716
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:35,560
But it still comes down to them deciding to some extent what they really want to do

717
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:39,240
And when they get there, what they want to do when they get there.

718
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:43,080
You know Tom's kind of. you know, wait until this weekend,

719
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:46,440
Blazer, are these guys on their way to first class? yet

720
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:48,920
My high ethical scout is only second class.

721
00:33:48,920 --> 00:33:55,000
You and your leaders are still doing some of the first day, not tying that kind of thing.

722
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,520
Yes, it's, I'm doing a lot of it.

723
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:59,879
Are you turning over the camp stoves to them,

724
00:33:59,879 --> 00:34:01,240
The cooking?

725
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:03,960
Have they been shopping on their own?

726
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:06,040
Have their patrols been shopping?

727
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:09,000
The patrols haven't been shopping.

728
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,520
We're only a single patrol unit.

729
00:34:10,520 --> 00:34:12,759
We have been letting individual scouts,

730
00:34:12,759 --> 00:34:14,840
particularly as they're working on second class requirements.

731
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:16,280
I've been letting them do the shopping.

732
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:17,560
Yeah,

733
00:34:17,560 --> 00:34:21,320
One thing you might try is send the whole patrol to the grocery store together

734
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:22,520
and let them shop together,

735
00:34:22,520 --> 00:34:26,679
Even if one guy's in charge. let them work through that as a patrol.

736
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:30,679
I've always had my patrols go shopping together

737
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:36,199
And they go to the grocery store and they shop and then during the camp out

738
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:38,040
then they cook their meals.

739
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:41,400
You know, someday you can spend about 80% of a day just making meals,

740
00:34:42,199 --> 00:34:45,239
But that's the level that they're at,

741
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:48,360
But they end up doing it themselves.

742
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:50,440
Blazer, is this useful for you?

743
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:51,320
It is actually.

744
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:55,159
But again, at the same point, I just let the boys just do ramen noodles,

745
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:59,080
Because that could very well happen, because that's just easy for them.

746
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:03,880
There's only one or two of them that want to spend a lot of time cooking.

747
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:10,920
Yeah, well, that's where you push them a little bit to raise the level. when you can

748
00:35:10,920 --> 00:35:12,600
Encourage the patrol leader.

749
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:19,160
And in your young group, can you start seeing one of the scouts that is

750
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:24,359
more handy with first aid or maybe with the knots,

751
00:35:24,359 --> 00:35:28,279
Or can you start recognizing some of those that with a little encouragement

752
00:35:28,279 --> 00:35:33,879
they may can take it a little further, because they all have to do the edge method at some point.

753
00:35:33,879 --> 00:35:40,120
Get them zeroing in on a specific skill, like the cooking guys, the ones that really like to cook.

754
00:35:40,120 --> 00:35:43,240
Get them teaching first-class cooking.

755
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:46,360
We're getting ready to accept weeblos into the troop

756
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:50,360
And I'm not sure how much they're.

757
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:53,000
I keep telling them the boys are going to have to do the teaching

758
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:55,560
and they don't seem to be very interested in that.

759
00:35:55,560 --> 00:35:56,600
They just want to have fun.

760
00:35:57,560 --> 00:35:59,800
Let me push back at you a little bit, Tom and Larry,

761
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:03,560
because we are talking about some 11 and 12-year-old boys.

762
00:36:03,560 --> 00:36:08,760
One of the messages that we often hear is they have to make a determination.

763
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:10,120
They get to do what they want to do.

764
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:14,759
Well, what the 11 and 12-year-old boys seem to want to do is they want to play basketball,

765
00:36:14,759 --> 00:36:17,799
or they want to play Chase Me or something like that.

766
00:36:17,799 --> 00:36:22,359
They don't seem to want to do this scouting business very much,

767
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:25,319
or at least what we would like to have them do in it.

768
00:36:26,359 --> 00:36:27,319
How do you work that?

769
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:29,240
Well, I think Larry said it-

770
00:36:30,359 --> 00:36:33,720
You just keep coaching them in the right direction.

771
00:36:33,720 --> 00:36:35,640
Well, basketball is not scouting.

772
00:36:35,640 --> 00:36:38,520
I mean, there's nothing wrong with a scout troop playing basketball occasionally,

773
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:43,000
and you just have to kind of get right down there with the patrol leader and

774
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:44,520
laying it out for them.

775
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:47,160
This is kind of where I'm going and where we're going.

776
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:50,440
They need to kind of latch on to that.

777
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:52,520
Yeah, you got a little bit of a challenge.

778
00:36:52,520 --> 00:36:54,280
The guys aren't really stepping up.

779
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:58,440
When we did have the extra meeting, the pizza worked beautifully.

780
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:02,520
The boys sort of. I think they were a little sheepish that they hadn't really

781
00:37:02,520 --> 00:37:03,720
gotten the sled done.

782
00:37:03,720 --> 00:37:07,160
But the next meeting they learned how to do their parts.

783
00:37:07,399 --> 00:37:12,200
The leaders were ready, but the boys came prepared to get the sled finished

784
00:37:12,200 --> 00:37:16,359
because they knew there was a deadline and we actually just used the sled this past weekend

785
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:17,240
and it held together

786
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:19,000
And I was happy with that.

787
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:20,440
Well, yeah, you're there.

788
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:23,799
I mean, you got a little bit of it and food is always good.

789
00:37:24,759 --> 00:37:25,799
Larry's a feeder.

790
00:37:25,799 --> 00:37:26,920
I feed them all the time.

791
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:36,920
The adults may be more involved as the coach and getting them to

792
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,360
understand what's going on.

793
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:45,080
But don't just give it to the scouts and then let them continue on with it.

794
00:37:45,080 --> 00:37:51,000
But you're always real close to them, coaching them so that they still understand,

795
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:54,120
because they don't understand what's supposed to happen yet

796
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:58,920
You may want to start introducing some challenges.

797
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,120
Have you been backpacking yet?

798
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:02,920
We've talked about it.

799
00:38:03,640 --> 00:38:04,120
Okay,

800
00:38:04,120 --> 00:38:09,000
Several of the boys actually used Clark Green's list for Christmas

801
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,680
and several of the boys did get backpacks.

802
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:15,480
Okay, well, backpacking, canoeing, there's those challenges.

803
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:18,920
I mean Clark, he goes to Switzerland, goes to Canada and I don't even go there.

804
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:25,880
But if you can get them pointed to now that they're getting some basic skills,

805
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:30,280
kind of the idea of taking on a slightly bigger challenge-

806
00:38:30,920 --> 00:38:34,680
I've often wondered if it would be a good idea to say,

807
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:38,680
okay, how do you go from here to the next town over?

808
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:41,960
Tell me how you do that and let them describe that,

809
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:46,040
Because a lot of times they just don't know how to get out of town.

810
00:38:46,680 --> 00:38:49,640
So, how are they going to go to Fillmont or go to?

811
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:54,120
let's get out of town first and see if they can figure that one out,

812
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:59,160
But practice with small steps and then keep moving up to the bigger steps.

813
00:39:00,280 --> 00:39:02,360
How are you getting on with the guys?

814
00:39:02,360 --> 00:39:04,360
I mean, you're the scout master, right?

815
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:05,400
Yes,

816
00:39:06,120 --> 00:39:15,560
And when you in the evenings, when you sit down after dinner, who makes the campfire?

817
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:17,320
The boys do

818
00:39:18,040 --> 00:39:22,600
Okay, and then the whole troupe, the boys and you guys, you adults, sit around

819
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:25,320
and talk and tell stories,

820
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:29,960
And usually just the adults. the kids are usually off doing flashlight tag-

821
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:34,760
And I just finished, they don't want to. our boys just want to go off and have

822
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:38,200
a flashlight tag or go to the graveyard or something like that.

823
00:39:38,200 --> 00:39:42,120
But I'm going to have to try to push that a little bit in that direction. also.

824
00:39:42,120 --> 00:39:43,960
Let me jump in for a second.

825
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:48,520
I think a lot of times what we're really far away from- and what I'm saying-

826
00:39:48,520 --> 00:39:54,920
so I'm talking about Larry and Tom and I are far away from- is being in that position

827
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:58,120
where you have a group of guys who are 11 or 12 years old.

828
00:39:58,120 --> 00:40:00,759
We're dealing with a couple of things that Blaze is not dealing with.

829
00:40:00,759 --> 00:40:02,759
First of all, we're dealing with some older scouts,

830
00:40:03,480 --> 00:40:05,080
And that's a big deal,

831
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:09,560
And we're also dealing with units that have been around for a long time

832
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:13,160
and have a lot of things that are kind of on autopilot.

833
00:40:13,160 --> 00:40:17,480
I think one of the important things for us to think about-

834
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:19,560
and I think that would be helpful for you too, Blaze-

835
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:21,880
is the kind of scale that you're dealing with

836
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:24,600
When you're talking about a guy who's 11 or 12 years old

837
00:40:24,600 --> 00:40:26,440
and you're just forming a troop and everything,

838
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:28,920
which is really exciting, by the way

839
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,319
What you would like to see them pay attention to,

840
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:35,799
instead of being at 15 or 20 minutes or an hour or whatever.

841
00:40:35,799 --> 00:40:38,520
they're going to pay attention to that for about five minutes

842
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:44,040
And then they need to run off about 40 minutes worth of steam

843
00:40:44,040 --> 00:40:46,200
And then you got another five minutes.

844
00:40:47,799 --> 00:40:48,839
I mean, does that make sense?

845
00:40:49,799 --> 00:40:51,720
That makes a lot more sense

846
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:53,799
And I know I've been mostly trying to emphasize

847
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:57,080
that the boys are having fun and let them do what they can do.

848
00:40:57,720 --> 00:41:00,440
I've been really happy that within the past month

849
00:41:00,440 --> 00:41:02,760
all eight boys have done something or so.

850
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:05,160
So none of my boys, they're all staying active

851
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:07,000
And when we've got a bunch of weeblos

852
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:08,760
that are going to be interested in coming over.

853
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,440
So I think I'm doing what I can,

854
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:13,320
But at the same point, I think it's

855
00:41:13,320 --> 00:41:14,680
somewhat a weeble of three program

856
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:17,400
because I don't have any older boys.

857
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:19,640
Well, that's okay if they're sticking with it.

858
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:20,440
That's a good plan

859
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:21,720
And you're moving forward,

860
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:25,080
but it's going to be in smaller increments than you would like.

861
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:25,320
Yes,

862
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:27,400
That is aggravating.

863
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:29,320
Yeah, but don't stop.

864
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,480
Don't stop looking forward.

865
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:34,200
Don't institutionalize where you're at now,

866
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:36,200
Because a year and a half from now

867
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:37,800
you're not going to be there anymore

868
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:39,800
If these eight guys stick with it

869
00:41:39,800 --> 00:41:41,800
and take these new weeblos on a year,

870
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:43,240
a year and a half from now,

871
00:41:43,240 --> 00:41:44,600
you're going to be a scout troop.

872
00:41:44,600 --> 00:41:46,040
I mean you're going to be there

873
00:41:46,040 --> 00:41:49,960
If you just stick with the plan. that's my goal.

874
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:53,720
We're looking at this from a really different perspective.

875
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:57,000
People who have a smaller troop or a younger troop.

876
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,880
I think the broad underlying concepts work,

877
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:02,120
but sometimes the application isn't as simple

878
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:03,800
as we would like to think it is.

879
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:05,480
It's a much longer process,

880
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:07,480
Much smaller steps.

881
00:42:08,120 --> 00:42:08,440
Yeah,

882
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:09,960
I don't know, Blaze.

883
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:12,840
Sometimes you just have to kind of have faith

884
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:14,600
that the program works,

885
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:17,080
Just keep hanging in there, because you know

886
00:42:17,080 --> 00:42:19,400
we don't like calling it a failure anymore.

887
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:21,080
You know a bad PLC meeting

888
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:23,880
or we didn't get our Condyke Derby sled

889
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:25,640
quite done, or whatever.

890
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,720
But they're not really failures

891
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,560
if they learn something from it

892
00:42:29,560 --> 00:42:33,720
and if they become motivated the next time.

893
00:42:33,720 --> 00:42:36,360
There's nothing like a failure quote

894
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:39,560
to actually organize a bunch of kids' heads

895
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:41,560
and getting straightened out,

896
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:43,880
And I'm thinking at this point

897
00:42:43,880 --> 00:42:45,880
now is the time I've got to push them a little.

898
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:47,800
The other advantage that we have on you

899
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:50,040
is that we've seen this work before

900
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,760
and you really haven't seen it work yet.

901
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:53,480
Yeah,

902
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:56,520
That, and hopefully we can share

903
00:42:56,520 --> 00:42:58,280
the encouragement with you that,

904
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:00,520
oh yeah, it will generally work.

905
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:01,480
You don't think it will

906
00:43:01,480 --> 00:43:01,960
Correct.

907
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:03,240
I mean, Tom's been sitting around

908
00:43:03,240 --> 00:43:05,000
on pins and needles for the past two weeks

909
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,680
wondering if he's going to get to go skiing

910
00:43:06,680 --> 00:43:08,280
or go to the- what is it?

911
00:43:08,280 --> 00:43:09,480
The Camperie,

912
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,280
Camperie, yeah,

913
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:11,480
Yeah, get to it.

914
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:15,640
There is an element of faith to it all,

915
00:43:16,359 --> 00:43:19,640
especially in the circumstance

916
00:43:19,640 --> 00:43:21,160
where you have absolutely no evidence

917
00:43:21,160 --> 00:43:23,240
that anything you're doing is working very well.

918
00:43:24,680 --> 00:43:28,440
There will be, like these little watershed events

919
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:31,480
that happen and you've got a bunch of guys

920
00:43:31,480 --> 00:43:33,560
interested in the troop right now. right,

921
00:43:33,560 --> 00:43:35,560
Well, right now I'm eight,

922
00:43:35,560 --> 00:43:37,240
I'm going to for sure. I've got 12,

923
00:43:37,240 --> 00:43:39,560
and I'm hoping to get maybe 16 or so.

924
00:43:40,120 --> 00:43:41,319
Yeah, well, I'll tell you

925
00:43:41,319 --> 00:43:43,319
if the boys are having a great time.

926
00:43:43,880 --> 00:43:46,760
you know it's going to go like gangbusters.

927
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:49,480
You know, Blaise, I think the secret

928
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:53,160
is around. what Clark was saying

929
00:43:53,160 --> 00:43:57,400
is that you're going to reap the reward

930
00:43:57,400 --> 00:43:58,600
by sticking through this.

931
00:43:59,320 --> 00:44:02,920
You know, when one of those guys is 14,, 15,, 16,

932
00:44:02,920 --> 00:44:06,280
and you hand his eagle badge to his mom to pin on him,

933
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:08,440
or you're sitting there at a camp out

934
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:10,680
and he's six feet tall

935
00:44:10,680 --> 00:44:12,920
and he walks over to some 11-year-old kid

936
00:44:13,480 --> 00:44:15,880
that's. you know, not even as far along

937
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:17,240
as the guys you've got-

938
00:44:17,240 --> 00:44:20,360
and sits down next to him, pulls out a scout book

939
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:22,120
and starts going through stuff-

940
00:44:22,120 --> 00:44:23,880
and you didn't say a word to either one of them.

941
00:44:24,440 --> 00:44:27,320
or you know, I could go through a thousand examples

942
00:44:27,320 --> 00:44:29,480
like that- and you're going to be sitting there

943
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:32,040
across camp in your chair thinking to yourself:

944
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:34,120
this is working.

945
00:44:34,120 --> 00:44:38,040
You know what Clark said just a second ago:

946
00:44:38,600 --> 00:44:40,200
this thing is working,

947
00:44:40,200 --> 00:44:42,600
This thing is happening and I am watching it.

948
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:44,920
And yeah, it was a pain

949
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:49,640
and I was tied up in knots occasionally about it,

950
00:44:49,640 --> 00:44:52,440
but when I saw the opportunity to back off

951
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,360
and let go and give it to them

952
00:44:55,080 --> 00:44:57,640
and they took it, it happened

953
00:44:57,640 --> 00:44:59,799
And at that moment you'll know,

954
00:44:59,799 --> 00:45:01,960
you will know that you're there

955
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:05,240
and you've seen it and from there

956
00:45:05,240 --> 00:45:06,120
you can't go back.

957
00:45:06,920 --> 00:45:08,120
You know, even if you start over

958
00:45:08,120 --> 00:45:09,480
with another eight weeblos,

959
00:45:09,480 --> 00:45:12,279
it'll be so ingrained in your mind.

960
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,440
I'm seeing glimmers, certainly,

961
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:17,800
but it's sort of like having a meeting

962
00:45:17,800 --> 00:45:19,080
where I think everything's going great

963
00:45:19,080 --> 00:45:20,440
and then a meeting where everything

964
00:45:20,440 --> 00:45:21,960
it seems like it's a lousy meeting.

965
00:45:23,480 --> 00:45:24,920
I have those all the time.

966
00:45:24,920 --> 00:45:26,280
Yeah, you've been visiting me.

967
00:45:26,920 --> 00:45:28,920
One thing I'll say over and over again:

968
00:45:28,920 --> 00:45:31,240
don't ever back off from letting them know

969
00:45:31,240 --> 00:45:33,080
that it's their job to lead, train

970
00:45:33,080 --> 00:45:34,760
and inspire those new weeblos.

971
00:45:35,400 --> 00:45:37,240
And even if they're only second class

972
00:45:37,240 --> 00:45:40,120
and they're barely 12, don't back off from that.

973
00:45:40,120 --> 00:45:41,560
You know that's their job:

974
00:45:41,560 --> 00:45:43,400
to bring those guys along.

975
00:45:43,400 --> 00:45:46,440
Just keep going at that, as strong as you can,

976
00:45:47,080 --> 00:45:49,240
taking care of those little guys.

977
00:45:49,240 --> 00:45:51,160
All the other stuff will take care of itself,

978
00:45:51,160 --> 00:45:53,080
both in the law, the program.

979
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:54,360
It'll all take care of itself.

980
00:45:55,080 --> 00:45:57,240
Well, they've told me they're not too excited,

981
00:45:57,240 --> 00:45:59,880
but actually we had three scouts come

982
00:45:59,880 --> 00:46:01,560
from another neighboring town

983
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:03,480
whose troop isn't doing very well either.

984
00:46:03,480 --> 00:46:05,640
but the three boys that came along

985
00:46:05,640 --> 00:46:07,880
were incorporated right into the activities

986
00:46:07,880 --> 00:46:09,720
in this past week.

987
00:46:10,360 --> 00:46:12,280
But when they say, hey, those little guys-

988
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:14,360
and they're not, you know, just tell them:

989
00:46:14,360 --> 00:46:15,480
guys, it's change

990
00:46:15,480 --> 00:46:17,640
And your boys? you don't like change

991
00:46:18,200 --> 00:46:20,200
And I know you're a little uncomfortable with it,

992
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:22,600
but it will be the best thing that you can do

993
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:24,440
for this scout troop.

994
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:27,640
Well, there's also a grand scouting tradition

995
00:46:27,640 --> 00:46:30,760
in older scouts complaining about the younger scouts.

996
00:46:30,760 --> 00:46:31,960
That's just,

997
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:32,760
It's a tradition.

998
00:46:33,320 --> 00:46:36,600
It is a hallowed tradition, Larry,

999
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:38,600
A hallowed tradition. yes,

1000
00:46:39,160 --> 00:46:40,920
It sounds like Blaise is.

1001
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:43,799
He's on the right trail.

1002
00:46:43,799 --> 00:46:44,920
You're on the right trail.

1003
00:46:46,279 --> 00:46:48,600
You can't focus too much on one particular.

1004
00:46:48,600 --> 00:46:49,720
You can't snapshot it.

1005
00:46:49,720 --> 00:46:51,720
You've got to look at the broad picture

1006
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:53,560
and see that it really is.

1007
00:46:54,759 --> 00:46:56,839
You're going in the right direction.

1008
00:46:57,720 --> 00:47:00,279
Yeah, I think we all agree about that.

1009
00:47:00,279 --> 00:47:01,480
Keep doing the right things

1010
00:47:01,480 --> 00:47:03,240
and the results will hit there.

1011
00:47:03,240 --> 00:47:05,799
As I say, I think I'm doing what I should be doing,

1012
00:47:05,799 --> 00:47:07,640
but at the same point, you always have these,

1013
00:47:07,640 --> 00:47:08,440
You always have to.

1014
00:47:08,440 --> 00:47:10,279
I think you always have to second guess yourself.

1015
00:47:10,279 --> 00:47:11,480
I would be more concerned

1016
00:47:11,480 --> 00:47:14,520
if you weren't having doubts and concerns about things,

1017
00:47:14,520 --> 00:47:17,799
especially since this is the first time through this.

1018
00:47:17,799 --> 00:47:19,879
That's to me as an indication of somebody

1019
00:47:19,879 --> 00:47:21,480
who's a decent leader.

1020
00:47:21,480 --> 00:47:23,240
That always is an indication.

1021
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:23,879
I just try

1022
00:47:24,520 --> 00:47:25,240
And we all do.

1023
00:47:25,240 --> 00:47:26,279
That's what we're all doing.

1024
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:28,200
Is your boy in there, Blaise?

1025
00:47:28,920 --> 00:47:29,560
Yes,

1026
00:47:29,560 --> 00:47:30,600
And that's the other thing.

1027
00:47:31,160 --> 00:47:33,480
You're always torn between how much you push him

1028
00:47:34,279 --> 00:47:35,240
Right.

1029
00:47:35,240 --> 00:47:36,279
That's another subject.

1030
00:47:36,280 --> 00:47:40,440
I tell you when you drop your son off at college

1031
00:47:41,080 --> 00:47:44,440
and he comes home a few months later and he goes.

1032
00:47:44,440 --> 00:47:46,840
